        "function": "document_download"
      },
      "severity": "high",
      "expected_category": "auth",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "manual_review",
        "cve_id": null,
        "description": "Resembles an IDOR/broken-access-control: DocumentVersion is fetched directly by the caller-controlled version_pk via get_object_or_404 (not scoped to the user's queryset) and then streamed back as a file download, which a scanner flags as object-reference access without authorization. It is actually SAFE: immediately after the lookup the view calls can_download_document(request.user, document) and raises PermissionDenied on failure. can_download_document (cases/authz.py:104) enforces role/tenant scope - firm admins allowed, staff must pass can_access_matter (matter_queryset_for ownership), and clients are restricted to documents on their own matter (portal_user_id == user.id) with CLIENT_SHARED/PUBLIC_FILING visibility. The view is also @login_required. So the direct-pk lookup is gated by an explicit ownership check."
      },
      "false_positive_trap": true,
      "campaign_id": "v2-campaign-1",
      "provider_run": "codex-high",
      "app": "legal-case-django"
    },
